Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat: one shared join of a role definition and
 Microsoft's per-action information

Get-RoleContext.ps1 links role-definitions/ and resource-actions/ by action name, without writing
anything to the snapshot. Per role: every action with its condition, description and isPrivileged
(null outside microsoft.directory); privilegedBecause, the actions Microsoft flags as sensitive,
which are the reason the role is privileged; privilegeCheck, whether the role flag agrees with its
actions (consistent, either mismatch, or unknown when data is missing); the inherited roles by
name; and every action without a description, listed. The backtest now uses this same join, so it
measures the routine on the production input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
